WEBVTT

1
00:00:49.633 --> 00:00:50.682
Ragnar!

2
00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.300
<i>Odin!</i>

3
00:03:04.051 --> 00:03:05.583
Ragnar!

4
00:04:40.364 --> 00:04:42.364
Come on. Let's go home.

5
00:04:50.491 --> 00:04:51.556
Watch.

6
00:05:23.023 --> 00:05:25.757
What are you two doing?

7
00:05:25.826 --> 00:05:28.693
I'm taking Bjorn to
the thing tomorrow.

8
00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:34.599
Not yet. He's not old enough.

9
00:05:34.668 --> 00:05:36.467
He's 12 years old.

10
00:05:36.536 --> 00:05:37.980
Take him next year.

11
00:05:38.004 --> 00:05:40.221
Next year is soon enough.

12
00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:42.841
He'll need a silk
ribbon. Lagertha.

13
00:05:46.647 --> 00:05:48.380
You're a handsome boy.

14
00:05:49.249 --> 00:05:50.465
Funny ears. though.

15
00:05:57.073 --> 00:06:00.658
Don't sleep with lots
of women in Kattegat.

16
00:06:00.727 --> 00:06:02.960
I can do without
it for a few days.

17
00:06:04.931 --> 00:06:08.451
Is that another way
of saying you love me?

18
00:06:10.803 --> 00:06:12.070
Huh?

19
00:06:12.139 --> 00:06:13.804
I always dream of you.

20
00:06:15.575 --> 00:06:18.943
Last night. I dreamt you were
feeding me blood pudding.

21
00:06:21.781 --> 00:06:24.115
What does that mean?

22
00:06:24.184 --> 00:06:26.784
It means you're
giving me your heart.

23
00:06:38.732 --> 00:06:39.897
Get your dog. boy.

24
00:06:39.966 --> 00:06:42.166
Frodi! Come on. boy.

25
00:06:57.484 --> 00:06:59.244
What will happen at the thing?

26
00:06:59.269 --> 00:07:02.482
The Earl will deal with
some criminal offenses.

27
00:07:02.506 --> 00:07:05.746
and then. we'll discuss
the summer raids.

28
00:07:06.409 --> 00:07:08.159
And where will you go?

29
00:07:08.228 --> 00:07:09.508
The Earl decides.

30
00:07:10.130 --> 00:07:11.630
He owns the ships.

31
00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:15.678
He'll send us to the east.

32
00:07:15.702 --> 00:07:17.782
as always. to the Baltic lands.

33
00:07:18.822 --> 00:07:21.050
but I want to know
what's to the west.

34
00:07:21.074 --> 00:07:24.120
What cities and
gods are over there.

35
00:07:24.144 --> 00:07:26.504
See. I'm not satisfied

36
00:07:27.047 --> 00:07:28.647
with this.

37
00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:36.721
Odin gave his eye
to acquire knowledge.

38
00:07:39.175 --> 00:07:41.275
but I would give far more.

39
00:07:46.149 --> 00:07:48.716
And will Earl Haraldson let you?

40
00:07:53.089 --> 00:07:54.622
Good.

41
00:07:55.709 --> 00:07:59.777
Like this. nice and tight.

42
00:07:59.846 --> 00:08:01.462
And on three.

43
00:08:02.332 --> 00:08:04.733
One. two. three.

44
00:08:06.653 --> 00:08:08.520
Very good. Gyda.

45
00:08:14.194 --> 00:08:16.110
Gyda. feed the goats.

46
00:08:18.348 --> 00:08:19.414
Go on!

47
00:08:22.886 --> 00:08:24.118
What do you want?

48
00:08:24.187 --> 00:08:25.931
We know you're all alone here.

49
00:08:25.955 --> 00:08:28.706
All the men are gone.

50
00:08:28.775 --> 00:08:32.109
If you're thirsty. I
will give you a drink.

51
00:08:32.178 --> 00:08:34.495
If you're hungry.
I will feed you.

52
00:08:34.564 --> 00:08:37.248
Otherwise. you must go.

53
00:08:37.317 --> 00:08:41.169
We will eat and drink after
we've satisfied our other needs.

54
00:08:53.133 --> 00:08:55.600
I don't want to kill you. woman.

55
00:08:55.669 --> 00:08:58.986
You couldn't kill me if
you tried for 100 years.

56
00:09:18.124 --> 00:09:19.373
Out!

57
00:09:27.668 --> 00:09:30.468
I went to confess
my love to her.

58
00:09:30.520 --> 00:09:32.220
but I was set upon by a bear

59
00:09:32.289 --> 00:09:36.441
and an enormous hound
who guarded her home.

60
00:09:36.493 --> 00:09:41.112
I killed the bear with my spear.

61
00:09:41.164 --> 00:09:44.398
and I managed to strangle
the hound with my bare hands.

62
00:09:46.853 --> 00:09:50.354
And that is how I gained
her hand in marriage.

63
00:09:51.858 --> 00:09:54.241
Did she tell you the same story?

64
00:09:56.930 --> 00:09:58.396
Just about.

65
00:10:06.139 --> 00:10:09.974
Are you ready to receive your
arm ring and become a man?

66
00:10:10.476 --> 00:10:11.809
Yes.

67
00:10:11.878 --> 00:10:13.327
And what does a man do?

68
00:10:15.499 --> 00:10:16.831
He fights.

69
00:10:17.266 --> 00:10:18.332
And?

70
00:10:19.536 --> 00:10:21.896
He looks after his family.

71
00:10:22.806 --> 00:10:24.655
That's right.

72
00:10:24.708 --> 00:10:27.042
Could you look after our family?

73
00:10:30.297 --> 00:10:33.298
What do you mean?
You look after us.

74
00:10:33.366 --> 00:10:34.966
Say I wasn't there.

75
00:10:37.504 --> 00:10:40.521
I have a big decision to make.

76
00:10:40.590 --> 00:10:42.791
It may change many things.

77
00:10:45.045 --> 00:10:48.963
Now. go to sleep. You
have a big day tomorrow.

78
00:12:16.485 --> 00:12:18.152
Bjorn!

79
00:12:20.807 --> 00:12:23.057
So. here you are. brother.

80
00:12:23.126 --> 00:12:24.409
Rollo.

81
00:12:24.461 --> 00:12:26.510
By Freyr and all the
gods. how you've grown.

82
00:12:26.579 --> 00:12:27.912
Hello. Rollo.

83
00:12:27.981 --> 00:12:31.349
Are you here for the thing?
You're a real man now.

84
00:12:31.418 --> 00:12:34.301
Come. let's get a drink.

85
00:12:42.512 --> 00:12:44.832
Looking a little pale. Bjorn.

86
00:12:46.515 --> 00:12:48.633
Why don't you go lie down?

87
00:12:54.390 --> 00:12:58.509
So where do you think the Earl
is going to send us this year?

88
00:12:58.578 --> 00:13:01.579
Those bastards to the
east are as poor as we are.

89
00:13:01.648 --> 00:13:02.947
I know.

90
00:13:05.785 --> 00:13:08.653
That's why we should sail west.

91
00:13:08.721 --> 00:13:10.571
I've heard such tales. Rollo.

92
00:13:10.639 --> 00:13:13.540
Great towns and
cities and treasures.

93
00:13:13.609 --> 00:13:17.194
Hoards of gold and
silver. and a new god.

94
00:13:17.263 --> 00:13:21.399
I've heard those stories.
too. but what does it mean?

95
00:13:21.467 --> 00:13:23.627
We can't sail across
an open ocean.

96
00:13:25.054 --> 00:13:28.455
I believe there's
a way to go west.

97
00:13:31.861 --> 00:13:35.963
I have something that
will change everything.

98
00:13:37.784 --> 00:13:38.849
What?

99
00:13:43.472 --> 00:13:45.690
What is that? Now just listen.

100
00:13:45.758 --> 00:13:47.841
A while back. I met someone.

101
00:13:48.778 --> 00:13:50.995
a wanderer.

102
00:13:51.064 --> 00:13:53.848
He told me it was
possible to go west.

103
00:13:53.916 --> 00:13:55.449
over the open sea.

104
00:13:56.469 --> 00:13:57.901
using this.

105
00:14:01.841 --> 00:14:04.259
It's a sun board.

106
00:14:04.327 --> 00:14:06.572
It needs to sit in water.

107
00:14:06.596 --> 00:14:08.729
Another wanderer?

108
00:14:08.798 --> 00:14:10.025
This time. it's different.

109
00:14:10.049 --> 00:14:12.734
Now tell me. Ragnar.
this wanderer of yours.

110
00:14:12.802 --> 00:14:14.513
has he ever sailed west himself?

111
00:14:14.537 --> 00:14:16.104
Just get some water.

112
00:14:30.320 --> 00:14:33.254
Now. this candle is the sun.

113
00:14:33.323 --> 00:14:37.975
Every day. the sun rises
up into the sky until noon.

114
00:14:38.044 --> 00:14:40.511
See how the shadow shortens?

115
00:14:40.580 --> 00:14:43.080
At noon. it is at its shortest.

116
00:14:43.149 --> 00:14:44.894
That only tells me how
far south I have traveled.

117
00:14:44.918 --> 00:14:47.284
Didn't I just tell
you to listen?

118
00:14:49.205 --> 00:14:52.874
The day before sailing. you
mark a circle around the pointer

119
00:14:52.942 --> 00:14:56.177
where the shadow is
at its shortest at noon.

120
00:14:56.246 --> 00:14:58.162
The next day at sea.

121
00:14:58.231 --> 00:15:00.965
you place the board back
into water around noon

122
00:15:01.033 --> 00:15:02.466
and watch the shadow.

123
00:15:03.936 --> 00:15:06.537
If the shadow only
touches the circle...

124
00:15:06.605 --> 00:15:08.284
Your course remains true?

125
00:15:08.308 --> 00:15:09.624
Yes.

126
00:15:09.692 --> 00:15:13.694
And if it passes outside
the circle. like this...

127
00:15:13.763 --> 00:15:17.798
Then you have drifted. and
you must steer further south.

128
00:15:17.867 --> 00:15:19.566
Yes.

129
00:15:19.635 --> 00:15:22.486
And what if it never
reaches the circle?

130
00:15:22.538 --> 00:15:25.150
Then you are too far south.
and must steer more to the north.

131
00:15:25.174 --> 00:15:27.475
That's it!

132
00:15:27.543 --> 00:15:30.928
Keep the noon
shadow on the circle.

133
00:15:30.997 --> 00:15:32.730
and your course will be true.

134
00:15:32.799 --> 00:15:34.365
West.

135
00:15:40.106 --> 00:15:42.206
But what if there is no sun?

136
00:15:42.275 --> 00:15:44.692
How can the board help you then?

137
00:15:44.760 --> 00:15:47.200
How could you find your way?

138
00:15:51.400 --> 00:15:52.650
Using this.

139
00:15:57.790 --> 00:15:59.256
Follow me outside.

140
00:16:04.697 --> 00:16:06.657
They call it a sunstone.

141
00:16:10.770 --> 00:16:11.969
You see?

142
00:16:12.906 --> 00:16:14.806
There is the sun.

143
00:16:14.874 --> 00:16:16.808
Now we go west.

144
00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:23.150
Come on. Come on.

145
00:16:39.265 --> 00:16:40.942
Silence!

146
00:16:40.966 --> 00:16:42.783
Silence!

147
00:17:02.072 --> 00:17:07.608
Olaf Anwend. you have pleaded
guilty to the charge of stealing.

148
00:17:07.676 --> 00:17:09.994
Tomorrow. you will
run a gauntlet of stones

149
00:17:10.063 --> 00:17:12.079
and turf as punishment.

150
00:17:13.299 --> 00:17:16.083
Yes. Lord. Thank you. Lord.

151
00:17:16.152 --> 00:17:18.586
Let it be known.
a fine is to be paid

152
00:17:18.671 --> 00:17:22.906
by anyone who fails
to throw something.

153
00:17:25.128 --> 00:17:27.028
Bring in the next accused.

154
00:17:29.148 --> 00:17:31.165
There he is! - Murderer!

155
00:17:31.901 --> 00:17:34.368
Burn him!

156
00:17:34.437 --> 00:17:37.805
Eric Trygvasson. you
are accused of the murder

157
00:17:37.890 --> 00:17:41.108
of Sigvald Strut this January.

158
00:17:42.178 --> 00:17:43.610
How do you plead?

159
00:17:43.679 --> 00:17:46.447
It wasn't murder. Lord. I
killed him in self-defense.

160
00:17:46.516 --> 00:17:48.349
Liar!

161
00:17:49.819 --> 00:17:51.034
If it wasn't murder.

162
00:17:51.103 --> 00:17:52.669
why did you not
declare your crime

163
00:17:52.738 --> 00:17:55.055
to the first person that
you met afterwards.

164
00:17:55.124 --> 00:17:57.174
as the law obliges?

165
00:17:57.243 --> 00:18:03.180
In fact. you passed by several
houses before you reported it.

166
00:18:03.249 --> 00:18:07.085
I thought the relatives of the
dead man might be living in them.

167
00:18:09.372 --> 00:18:14.542
The law allows you to pass two
houses. in such circumstances.

168
00:18:14.611 --> 00:18:16.043
but never a third.

169
00:18:16.112 --> 00:18:18.190
You murdered my
brother in cold blood!

170
00:18:18.214 --> 00:18:20.247
It's not true!

171
00:18:20.316 --> 00:18:24.384
We argued about some disputed
land. He pulled out a knife!

172
00:18:24.453 --> 00:18:26.965
You wanted that
land for yourself!

173
00:18:26.989 --> 00:18:29.907
You're a liar and a coward.

174
00:18:29.976 --> 00:18:32.843
Who says I'm a
coward? I'm not a coward.

175
00:18:33.863 --> 00:18:35.279
Silence!

176
00:18:36.915 --> 00:18:39.816
As the normal procedures
were not followed.

177
00:18:39.885 --> 00:18:43.137
this killing cannot
be atoned for

178
00:18:43.206 --> 00:18:46.023
by compensating
the victim's family.

179
00:18:46.091 --> 00:18:50.210
Murder is a dishonorable
deed amongst our people.

180
00:18:50.279 --> 00:18:54.181
Carried out in secret.
unacknowledged.

181
00:18:54.250 --> 00:18:57.518
and likely to give rise to
a series of revenge killings

182
00:18:57.587 --> 00:19:00.521
that would involve
your own family.

183
00:19:02.008 --> 00:19:05.192
Lord. you knew about that land.

184
00:19:05.261 --> 00:19:08.301
You knew I had a
claim to it... Enough!

185
00:19:08.531 --> 00:19:11.165
I ask you to look
to the accused.

186
00:19:12.718 --> 00:19:14.468
If you think that he is guilty.

187
00:19:15.572 --> 00:19:16.938
raise your arms.

188
00:19:30.470 --> 00:19:32.786
The decision must be unanimous.

189
00:19:43.950 --> 00:19:45.315
Eric Trygvasson.

190
00:19:46.819 --> 00:19:49.436
you have been
found guilty of murder.

191
00:19:49.505 --> 00:19:51.345
Yes! MAN 2: Justice!

192
00:19:51.657 --> 00:19:53.174
How do you wish to die?

193
00:19:55.694 --> 00:19:58.612
By beheading. Lord.

194
00:19:58.680 --> 00:20:02.583
Your wish is granted. You
shall be executed tomorrow.

195
00:20:04.703 --> 00:20:08.072
After which we shall feast and
talk about the summer raids.

196
00:20:27.960 --> 00:20:29.477
You have to.

197
00:21:09.802 --> 00:21:12.770
Why is he smiling. Father?

198
00:21:12.838 --> 00:21:16.023
He wants to die
well. without fear.

199
00:21:16.792 --> 00:21:18.575
to atone for his sins.

200
00:21:28.938 --> 00:21:32.205
You must watch. for his sake.

201
00:21:32.292 --> 00:21:35.225
It's his only hope
of reaching Valhalla.

202
00:21:51.060 --> 00:21:52.693
Feed him to your pigs!

203
00:21:56.114 --> 00:21:58.698
And I curse him.

204
00:21:58.767 --> 00:22:01.669
May he never enter Valhalla.

205
00:22:01.737 --> 00:22:04.387
May he never
feast with the gods.

206
00:22:09.829 --> 00:22:11.128
Why did he do that?

207
00:22:11.197 --> 00:22:14.131
He should not have done that.

208
00:22:14.199 --> 00:22:16.378
Someone told me he
wanted that land for himself.

209
00:22:16.402 --> 00:22:18.280
and he knew Trygvasson
had the best claim to it.

210
00:22:18.304 --> 00:22:19.544
but refused to sell it.

211
00:22:21.941 --> 00:22:25.810
You hear that. boy? This is
how things are done around here.

212
00:22:30.066 --> 00:22:32.499
Olaf. son of Ingolf.

213
00:22:32.568 --> 00:22:35.235
Bjorn. son of Ragnar.

214
00:22:35.304 --> 00:22:40.040
may you accept this
gift of salt and earth

215
00:22:40.109 --> 00:22:45.346
to remind yourself that you
belong to both the land and the sea.

216
00:22:53.288 --> 00:22:59.459
These arm rings bind you in
loyalty to me. your lord. your chieftain.

217
00:22:59.528 --> 00:23:04.230
Any oath that you swear on these
rings must be honored and kept.

218
00:23:04.299 --> 00:23:06.066
Do you understand
and swear to this?

219
00:23:06.135 --> 00:23:07.984
Yes. Lord. Yes. Lord.

220
00:23:08.054 --> 00:23:12.006
And do you freely give your fealty
to me. your lord. your chieftain?

221
00:23:12.074 --> 00:23:13.754
Yes. Lord. Yes. Lord.

222
00:23:15.878 --> 00:23:19.630
Good. You may
put on the arm rings.

223
00:23:26.221 --> 00:23:27.771
Come here.

224
00:23:53.949 --> 00:23:55.448
Let us feast!

225
00:23:55.517 --> 00:23:56.750
My Lord.

226
00:23:58.420 --> 00:24:00.587
we all want to feast.

227
00:24:00.656 --> 00:24:03.990
but we also want to know where
we will be raiding this summer.

228
00:24:04.910 --> 00:24:07.060
Can't it wait. Ragnar?

229
00:24:07.129 --> 00:24:09.063
No. Tell us.

230
00:24:09.148 --> 00:24:11.181
We want to know.

231
00:24:11.250 --> 00:24:13.095
We have a right to know.

232
00:24:13.119 --> 00:24:14.968
Very well.

233
00:24:15.037 --> 00:24:19.456
We will raid east again. to
the eastlands and into Russia.

234
00:24:19.525 --> 00:24:20.991
Every year

235
00:24:22.394 --> 00:24:24.094
we go to the same places!

236
00:24:27.867 --> 00:24:30.066
But there is an alternative.

237
00:24:32.871 --> 00:24:34.071
if you choose.

238
00:24:36.692 --> 00:24:40.694
Yes. yes. Choice. yes.

239
00:24:40.763 --> 00:24:44.498
I have heard of these
rumors. these stories.

240
00:24:44.566 --> 00:24:48.318
That if we travel west. that
we will somehow reach a land

241
00:24:48.387 --> 00:24:50.370
that is rich and plentiful.

242
00:24:52.842 --> 00:24:58.012
But I tell you that I will not
risk my ships or my reputation

243
00:24:58.080 --> 00:25:00.180
on such a deluded fantasy.

244
00:25:02.284 --> 00:25:05.119
They are my ships.
I pay for them.

245
00:25:05.187 --> 00:25:08.121
And they go where
I tell them to go.

246
00:25:08.190 --> 00:25:10.374
Now that's the
end of the matter.

247
00:25:15.364 --> 00:25:16.697
Let's feast!

248
00:25:30.780 --> 00:25:32.379
Let me see!

249
00:25:34.750 --> 00:25:36.366
It's a fine ring.

250
00:25:42.391 --> 00:25:45.242
Ragnar Lothbrok.

251
00:25:45.311 --> 00:25:49.113
Earl Haraldson wants to
speak with you in private.

252
00:25:51.968 --> 00:25:53.584
Stay with your uncle.

253
00:26:06.214 --> 00:26:08.114
Ragnar Lothbrok.

254
00:26:11.620 --> 00:26:12.853
Sit down.

255
00:26:18.594 --> 00:26:20.444
Are you hungry?

256
00:26:21.881 --> 00:26:23.196
Yes. Lord.

257
00:26:28.154 --> 00:26:30.487
You want to feast in my hall?

258
00:26:30.556 --> 00:26:33.089
You want to sail in my ships?

259
00:26:33.158 --> 00:26:34.958
Anything else you want from me?

260
00:26:36.512 --> 00:26:37.544
Lord...

261
00:26:37.613 --> 00:26:40.797
You keep talking about the west.

262
00:26:40.866 --> 00:26:43.733
What do you know of it? Hmm?

263
00:26:43.802 --> 00:26:47.787
Why are you so certain
that it's a land of great riches?

264
00:26:48.690 --> 00:26:50.057
I can't be sure.

265
00:26:51.359 --> 00:26:52.537
But I believe that...

266
00:26:52.561 --> 00:26:54.121
I don't care what you believe.

267
00:26:55.197 --> 00:26:58.331
You insulted me out there.

268
00:26:58.400 --> 00:27:01.318
and not for the first time.

269
00:27:01.386 --> 00:27:05.105
but. believe me.
it will be the last.

270
00:27:11.680 --> 00:27:13.696
Who told you you could go?

271
00:27:21.123 --> 00:27:23.724
You are a farmer.

272
00:27:25.360 --> 00:27:27.895
You should be
content with your lot.

273
00:27:29.665 --> 00:27:32.733
Farms are few and
in great demand.

274
00:27:34.386 --> 00:27:36.553
and there are many people here

275
00:27:36.622 --> 00:27:39.123
who would like to
possess your land.

276
00:27:41.861 --> 00:27:44.344
Do you understand
what I'm saying?

277
00:27:45.848 --> 00:27:49.049
I understand.

278
00:27:49.118 --> 00:27:52.870
Then don't ever stick
your nose in my face again.

279
00:28:07.052 --> 00:28:09.787
I don't trust him. Watch him.

280
00:28:22.785 --> 00:28:24.425
Where are they?

281
00:28:24.803 --> 00:28:26.169
Where are my sons?

282
00:28:26.238 --> 00:28:28.171
You said you'd found them.

283
00:29:13.018 --> 00:29:16.353
Where are we going
now? I'm so tired.

284
00:29:16.422 --> 00:29:17.754
To talk to the gods.

285
00:29:19.691 --> 00:29:21.158
It's what we do.

286
00:29:32.153 --> 00:29:34.554
Why don't you
come in? I'm waiting.

287
00:29:41.196 --> 00:29:42.395
Sit.

288
00:29:48.187 --> 00:29:50.454
What do you want?

289
00:29:50.522 --> 00:29:53.156
I want to know what
the gods have in store.

290
00:29:54.343 --> 00:29:57.377
For you. or for the boy?

291
00:29:58.613 --> 00:30:02.632
I'm more interested in myself.

292
00:30:02.701 --> 00:30:06.470
The gods desire you to
have a great future. I see that.

293
00:30:07.890 --> 00:30:12.225
But they can withdraw
their goodwill at any time.

294
00:30:12.294 --> 00:30:15.361
To have this great future.

295
00:30:15.447 --> 00:30:17.513
must I challenge the law?

296
00:30:17.582 --> 00:30:22.552
You must convince the
gods to alter the runes

297
00:30:23.956 --> 00:30:26.256
so they work in your favor.

298
00:30:26.992 --> 00:30:29.592
But the laws of men

299
00:30:29.661 --> 00:30:34.130
are far below the workings
and shapings of the gods.

300
00:30:36.968 --> 00:30:39.636
So I should take the laws of men

301
00:30:40.506 --> 00:30:42.105
into my own hands?

302
00:30:46.227 --> 00:30:47.994
Answer me.

303
00:30:48.063 --> 00:30:50.430
You already have your answer.

304
00:30:50.498 --> 00:30:54.000
No. I don't.

305
00:30:54.069 --> 00:30:57.303
Well. then go and
ask the gods yourself.

306
00:30:57.372 --> 00:30:59.372
What are you afraid of?

307
00:31:06.982 --> 00:31:08.315
Wait outside.

308
00:31:08.384 --> 00:31:09.650
All right.

309
00:31:11.052 --> 00:31:14.120
You haven't helped
me at all. ancient one.

310
00:31:17.709 --> 00:31:20.243
Perhaps you asked
the wrong questions.

311
00:31:40.165 --> 00:31:42.298
We have someone
special to visit.

312
00:31:42.367 --> 00:31:44.334
His name is Floki.

313
00:31:44.403 --> 00:31:46.019
"Floki"?

314
00:31:46.104 --> 00:31:48.738
Like Loki. the god?

315
00:31:48.807 --> 00:31:52.275
Yes. only different.

316
00:31:52.343 --> 00:31:54.210
How is he different?

317
00:31:54.279 --> 00:31:56.580
He's not a god.

318
00:31:56.632 --> 00:31:59.332
Why didn't he come to the thing?

319
00:31:59.400 --> 00:32:00.734
Because...

320
00:32:02.203 --> 00:32:03.737
Because he's shy.

321
00:32:10.362 --> 00:32:13.463
Floki. this is my son. Bjorn.

322
00:32:14.400 --> 00:32:17.133
Hello. How are you?

323
00:32:17.185 --> 00:32:19.402
Well. Thank you. sir.

324
00:32:20.722 --> 00:32:21.921
Let me see.

325
00:32:25.710 --> 00:32:28.478
You have your father's eyes

326
00:32:28.547 --> 00:32:30.163
unfortunately.

327
00:32:31.183 --> 00:32:33.133
Why unfortunately?

328
00:32:33.202 --> 00:32:35.352
It means he will be like you.

329
00:32:35.420 --> 00:32:38.187
and therefore he will
want to do better than you.

330
00:32:38.257 --> 00:32:40.256
and you will hate him for it.

331
00:32:43.194 --> 00:32:46.162
How can you tell that by
just looking at my face?

332
00:32:46.231 --> 00:32:48.276
It's the same with trees.

333
00:32:48.300 --> 00:32:50.211
I can tell which trees will make

334
00:32:50.235 --> 00:32:53.236
the best planks just
by looking at them.

335
00:32:53.305 --> 00:32:56.289
I can look inside the tree.

336
00:32:57.576 --> 00:32:59.809
Floki is a boat-builder.

337
00:32:59.878 --> 00:33:01.528
Among other things.

338
00:33:33.061 --> 00:33:35.595
This is one.

339
00:33:35.663 --> 00:33:38.576
Inside this tree are two
almost perfect planks.

340
00:33:38.600 --> 00:33:40.912
They will bend. then curve.

341
00:33:40.936 --> 00:33:43.614
like a woman's body
from the thighs to the back.

342
00:33:43.638 --> 00:33:47.340
When I split this
tree. I will find them.

343
00:33:49.410 --> 00:33:51.327
You can see that?

344
00:33:53.649 --> 00:33:55.930
Do you think I'm joking?

345
00:34:06.728 --> 00:34:11.347
I joke about many
things. son of Ragnar.

346
00:34:11.416 --> 00:34:14.651
but never about ship-building.

347
00:34:14.720 --> 00:34:18.705
Do you imagine ships
are just dead things?

348
00:34:18.773 --> 00:34:21.908
So. what about our boat?

349
00:34:26.181 --> 00:34:28.498
It will be lighter and
carry a bigger sail.

350
00:34:28.567 --> 00:34:29.961
The construction is different.

351
00:34:29.985 --> 00:34:31.996
It's built with a
strong central plank.

352
00:34:32.020 --> 00:34:33.653
The two strakes
above it are nailed

353
00:34:33.721 --> 00:34:35.033
directly onto the
knees of the frame.

354
00:34:35.057 --> 00:34:37.023
But the ones below... Look!

355
00:34:37.092 --> 00:34:39.876
Are cleated and lashed
onto the frames. not nailed.

356
00:34:39.944 --> 00:34:42.028
so they can move in
relation to each other.

357
00:34:42.097 --> 00:34:45.131
This means the boat won't butt
against the waves like a goat.

358
00:34:45.200 --> 00:34:48.101
but move over
them like a ripple.

359
00:34:48.170 --> 00:34:50.748
The hull is deeper. How
will my men set their oars?

360
00:34:50.772 --> 00:34:52.733
I will cut them into
the sheerstrakes.

361
00:34:52.757 --> 00:34:55.117
and the ports can be closed
when the boat is at sea.

362
00:34:55.177 --> 00:34:57.138
And you think it could
handle long sea voyages?

363
00:34:57.162 --> 00:34:59.796
That's why I'm building it.

364
00:35:03.101 --> 00:35:05.852
But will it be strong enough?

365
00:35:05.921 --> 00:35:08.021
We won't know that until we try.

366
00:35:10.658 --> 00:35:13.092
For the anchor.

367
00:35:13.161 --> 00:35:16.129
It's all I have left from
last summer's raids.

368
00:35:16.198 --> 00:35:17.914
Don't worry.

369
00:35:17.982 --> 00:35:21.100
We'll soon be as
rich as dwarves!

370
00:35:32.280 --> 00:35:34.147
I missed you.

371
00:35:42.407 --> 00:35:45.157
Did anything happen
while we were away?

372
00:35:47.763 --> 00:35:49.028
No.

373
00:35:53.635 --> 00:35:56.069
Did you miss me?

374
00:36:01.776 --> 00:36:04.194
I ached with love longing.

375
00:36:05.781 --> 00:36:08.381
My belly was empty of laughter.

376
00:36:09.517 --> 00:36:11.718
Is that what you want? Hmm?

377
00:36:16.642 --> 00:36:18.358
You want me to make you laugh?

378
00:36:20.378 --> 00:36:22.545
I don't want to laugh now.

379
00:36:25.484 --> 00:36:27.684
I want to ride you.

380
00:36:29.103 --> 00:36:30.343
like a bull.

381
00:36:33.508 --> 00:36:35.792
Like a wild bull.

382
00:37:02.554 --> 00:37:04.721
Hello. young Bjorn.

383
00:37:04.789 --> 00:37:06.238
Hello. Rollo.

384
00:37:06.307 --> 00:37:07.707
Where are your parents?

385
00:37:08.560 --> 00:37:10.627
They are having sex.

386
00:37:14.332 --> 00:37:15.832
Well...

387
00:37:17.301 --> 00:37:19.535
I guess we'll have to wait.

388
00:37:33.584 --> 00:37:36.168
So. Gyda.

389
00:37:36.237 --> 00:37:38.788
is your mother teaching
you how to use a shield?

390
00:37:38.856 --> 00:37:42.125
Yes. I know how to use a shield.

391
00:37:42.194 --> 00:37:44.739
Your mother was a
famous shield-maiden.

392
00:37:44.763 --> 00:37:45.790
Was?

393
00:37:45.814 --> 00:37:48.664
Is a famous shield-maiden.

394
00:37:48.733 --> 00:37:50.861
Come on. children. to bed.
- Do I have to?

395
00:37:50.885 --> 00:37:52.168
Let's leave the men.

396
00:37:52.236 --> 00:37:54.670
But I'm a man. I have a ring.

397
00:37:54.723 --> 00:37:56.539
Let him stay awhile.

398
00:37:56.608 --> 00:37:57.940
To bed!

399
00:38:00.779 --> 00:38:02.195
Say good night.

400
00:38:02.264 --> 00:38:03.874
Good night. my children.

401
00:38:03.898 --> 00:38:05.659
- Good night.
- Good night.

402
00:38:05.683 --> 00:38:07.028
Good night. Good night.

403
00:38:07.052 --> 00:38:08.318
Hey!

404
00:38:17.895 --> 00:38:19.929
Good night. Father.

405
00:38:21.966 --> 00:38:24.167
Tell me your news.

406
00:38:24.236 --> 00:38:26.218
What about the boat?

407
00:38:26.287 --> 00:38:27.987
It's nearly ready.

408
00:38:29.441 --> 00:38:32.091
I won't go under your command.

409
00:38:35.146 --> 00:38:37.563
I won't go unless
we're all equal.

410
00:38:38.467 --> 00:38:40.367
We are brothers.

411
00:38:42.270 --> 00:38:44.804
You and I will always be equal.

412
00:38:51.229 --> 00:38:53.596
Then we must find a crew.

413
00:38:53.665 --> 00:38:56.733
Not many men will go against
the wishes of Haraldson.

414
00:38:58.637 --> 00:39:00.402
Many will be afraid.

415
00:39:01.556 --> 00:39:04.791
Some may even go
to him and betray us.

416
00:39:07.896 --> 00:39:09.629
I must go piss.

417
00:39:42.947 --> 00:39:45.048
Yesterday. I was with
a girl from the town.

418
00:39:45.116 --> 00:39:46.116
Thank you.

419
00:39:46.968 --> 00:39:49.288
A good-looking girl. too.

420
00:39:54.458 --> 00:39:57.778
But when she
shouted out in pleasure.

421
00:39:58.796 --> 00:40:01.156
I didn't see her face.

422
00:40:03.034 --> 00:40:04.834
I saw yours.

423
00:40:07.304 --> 00:40:08.638
Lagertha...

424
00:40:10.341 --> 00:40:12.241
Don't talk like that.

425
00:40:12.309 --> 00:40:13.542
Why not?

426
00:40:15.981 --> 00:40:18.141
I think about you all the time.

427
00:40:19.200 --> 00:40:20.933
That's too bad.

428
00:40:22.854 --> 00:40:24.934
Don't insult me. shield-maiden.

429
00:40:25.373 --> 00:40:26.606
No.

430
00:40:26.674 --> 00:40:28.975
I would never insult you.

431
00:40:29.043 --> 00:40:31.544
You're too great a warrior.

432
00:40:35.082 --> 00:40:38.100
but perhaps not so great a man.

433
00:41:13.955 --> 00:41:15.487
I saw something.

434
00:41:16.641 --> 00:41:17.974
What did you see?

435
00:41:19.143 --> 00:41:21.110
A sign.

436
00:41:23.481 --> 00:41:26.215
It made me certain
we're doing the right thing.

437
00:41:34.459 --> 00:41:36.108
Good night. brother.

438
00:41:55.229 --> 00:41:56.629
Set the sail.

439
00:41:58.282 --> 00:42:00.616
Floki! The sail!

440
00:42:01.385 --> 00:42:02.601
She'll sink.

441
00:42:02.670 --> 00:42:04.169
No. she bloody won't.

442
00:42:04.238 --> 00:42:07.123
I shouldn't have pretended
to build such a boat.

443
00:42:07.191 --> 00:42:09.425
It's beyond my
humble capabilities.

444
00:42:11.162 --> 00:42:12.495
I'll set the sail.

445
00:42:13.298 --> 00:42:14.930
I'm sorry. Ragnar.

446
00:42:14.999 --> 00:42:17.266
I've wasted all your
money. It was all a joke.

447
00:42:17.335 --> 00:42:19.068
Shut up. man.

448
00:42:42.010 --> 00:42:43.109
Ha!

449
00:42:48.583 --> 00:42:50.833
Now it runs on its cool keel.

450
00:42:50.902 --> 00:42:52.835
It's beautiful.

451
00:42:52.904 --> 00:42:56.873
Why didn't you believe
me? I told you I could do it!

452
00:43:01.362 --> 00:43:04.997
Now it's all up to
you. Ragnar Lothbrok.
